Q: How do I capture the messages from a stored procedure call in ADO.NET? A: <p>I believe you can tap into the <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.data.sqlclient.sqlconnection.infomessage" rel="noreferrer">SqlConnection.InfoMessage</a> event in the <code>Microsoft.Data.SqlClient</code> namespace to get those notifications and inspect them / handle them.</p>
<pre><code>public event Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SqlInfoMessageEventHandler InfoMessage;
</code></pre>

Q: Rounding decimals in Swift, while maintaining a trailing zero A: <pre><code>@Test func rounding() {
    let num = Decimal(string: &quot;609.660345&quot;)!
    let round = num.roundedDecimal(to: 3)

    // 609660 * 10^-3
    let expected = Decimal(sign: .plus, exponent: -3, significand: 609660)

    #expect(round == expected)
}
</code></pre>
